SUMMARY, WHICH IS NOT THE LICENCE

Hail is free to download, read and use, for anything, including at work. It is
not open source: you may not change it, republish it, or sell it. The plugin
contract in src/Hail.Sdk, the plugin template in templates/hail-plugin and the
plugin guide in docs/plugins.md are the exception, and are MIT licensed so that
anyone can build and publish plugins. The terms below are what actually apply.


1. DEFINITIONS

"The Software" means the Hail source code, the compiled binaries built from
it, its assets, and its documentation, as published by the copyright holder,
except for the SDK.

"The SDK" means everything in the folder src/Hail.Sdk and the Hail.Sdk
package built from it, everything in the folder templates/hail-plugin, and the
file docs/plugins.md: what a plugin author compiles against, starts from, and
copies examples out of.

"You" means the individual or organisation exercising the permissions below.


